# Netlify redirects. Lives in public/ so it ships inside dist/ and works for
# every deploy method, including drag-and-drop.
#
# Pages from the previous multi-page site. The new site is one page, so each
# old URL is sent permanently (301) to where its content now lives: links and
# search results pointing at them land somewhere real, and Google replaces the
# old URL with the new one. Netlify matches with or without a trailing slash.
/what-we-do/  /#what-you-get  301!
/about/       /               301!
/lab/         /               301!

# The share image was renamed when it was redrawn; keep the old URL working.
/og-default.png  /og-image.png  301!
